    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Lateral sprain of the right ankle (S93.401A)</content>. A grade 2 inversion sprain of the anterior talofibular ligament. The Ottawa ankle rules are negative, so a fracture is very unlikely and no X-ray is needed. The toe graft is intact; the sprain is not related to the melanoma or the surgery. [S]<list><item>Lace-up ankle support; walk on it as pain allows; ice and elevation for two or three days.</item><item>Ibuprofen 400 mg three times daily with food for up to five days.</item><item>Ankle range and balance exercises from day 3; a physical therapy session for balance work if not improving in a week.</item><item>Back to football when he can hop and run figures of eight without pain, usually three to four weeks, with the ankle support.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acral melanoma of the right great toe, stage IA, after digit-sparing excision (C43.71)</content>. The graft is healed with no sign of recurrence and the groin is normal. [S]<list><item>Continue monthly self-examination.</item><item>Melanoma review in about two months as planned.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Melanoma: Cutaneous, Version 3.2026 (2026); Bachmann LM, et al. Accuracy of Ottawa ankle rules to exclude fractures of the ankle and mid-foot: systematic review. BMJ 2003;326(7386):417 (2003)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Return if he cannot bear weight, if pain or swelling worsen, or if the foot becomes numb or cold. Preventive visit next month as booked. Next scheduled visit 1977-09-21: periodic adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
